# --- data must never enter the repo ----------------------------------------
# The brief asks to exclude the data directory and any raw data file so that
# person-level data can never be pushed by accident.
data/
/data/**
*.csv
*.tsv
*.dta
*.parquet
*.RData
*.rdata
*.rds

# --- exceptions: the aggregate deliverables we DO want committed ------------
# A blanket *.csv ignore would also drop the codebook and the aggregate output
# tables, which are the point of the project. These are aggregates only (no
# person-level rows), so we force-add them back. Nothing else under output/ or
# docs/ is a raw data file.
!docs/codebook.csv
!output/*.csv

# --- laptop path (the path constant) ---------------------------------------
# R/config.R holds DATA_DIR for this laptop. Never committed. Each person keeps
# their own; R/config.example.R is the committed template.
R/config.R
.Renviron

# --- R / renv / RStudio ----------------------------------------------------
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/lock/
renv/python/
renv/sandbox/
renv/staging/

# --- OS noise --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# postings files are .csv.zip; block all zip archives too
*.zip
.positai
